(LIB-55 through LIB-58 -- calling a library from a non-Vox host. Builds
 the mathkit library, then a hand-written nasm+ld driver (LIB-driver.asm)
 calls its exports directly by their mangled labels, using the Vox
 calling convention: integer arguments in rdi, rsi, ...; result in rax.
 Reproduces LANGUAGE.md:5358-5394 verbatim except for the output filename.
 Ran, from the repo root, in a scratch directory:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm
   V=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox
   $V docs/ledger/probes/libraries/shared/LIB-driver.vox --shared -o libdriverlib.so
   nm -D --defined-only libdriverlib.so
   nasm -f elf64 -o LIB-driver.o docs/ledger/probes/libraries/shared/LIB-driver.asm
   ld -dynamic-linker /lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2 -rpath '$ORIGIN' \
      -o LIB-driver LIB-driver.o -L. -ldriverlib
   ./LIB-driver
 expected output:
   nm:
     000000000000072c T mathkit_1_0_add_two_numbers
     000000000000076c T mathkit_1_0_greet
   link: exit 0
   run:
     hello from mathkit
   (exit 0)
)

Library mathkit version "1.0".

To 'add two numbers' with a number called x and a number called y. Return a number, x add y.

To greet.
  Print "hello from mathkit".
